  whyItMatters: "Because Islamic banks' asset-side financing overwhelmingly creates debt (through Murabaha, Ijarah, Salam, Istisna'a and similar trade/lease modes), the rules in this chapter -- on what a loan may and may not carry, how defaults and insolvency are handled, how debt can (and cannot) be assigned or secured, and why debt cannot be sold or indexed -- directly govern the legal boundaries of everyday Islamic banking operations. Understanding these rules is essential to distinguishing legitimate debt-recovery and risk-management tools from disguised Riba.",
